---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Hainan Travel Guide 2026 — Visa-Free for 59 Countries';
const description = 'Plan your trip to Hainan, China tropical island. 30-day visa-free for 59 countries. Tropical beaches, rainforest hikes, local food, and travel tips in one guide.';
const lastUpdated = 'June 2026';
const readTime = '7 min';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">

    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/en/cities/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to City Guides
      </a>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">🏝️ Hainan</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        Hainan Travel Guide: China's Tropical Island — No Visa Needed for 59 Countries
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Beaches, rainforest, volcanoes, and world-class resorts — and citizens of 59 countries can visit without a visa for up to 30 days.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
        <span>⏱️ {readTime}</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Quick Answer -->
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-50 to-teal-50 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-6 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-900 mb-4">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-emerald-800 leading-relaxed"><strong>Hainan is China's tropical island paradise — beaches, rainforest, volcanoes, and world-class resorts — and citizens of 59 countries can visit without a visa for up to 30 days.</strong> No tour group needed, no embassy visit required. Fly into Haikou or Sanya with your passport and a return ticket, and you're in.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-8">This is a big deal if you're from the <strong>US, Mexico, Philippines, Indonesia, or Czech Republic</strong> — these countries aren't on China's mainland 30-day visa-free list. (<a href="/en/visa/visa-free/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">See the full 59-country list →</a>)</p>

    <!-- Quick Stats Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-12">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl mb-1">☀️</p>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Tropical Climate</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">Avg 24°C / 75°F year-round</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl mb-1">🏖️</p>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Top Beaches</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">Yalong Bay, Dadonghai, Haitang Bay</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl mb-1">🌋</p>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Volcanic Geopark</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">Haikou's unique geology</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl mb-1">🌴</p>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Rainforest</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">Wuzhishan, Yanoda, Bawangling</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl mb-1">⛳</p>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Golf Resorts</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">World-class courses</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4 border border-gray-100 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl mb-1">🦞</p>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Fresh Seafood</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">Hainan is famous for it</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Which Countries Qualify -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="visa-free-countries" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Which Countries Qualify for Hainan Visa-Free?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4"><strong>59 countries</strong> — mostly the same as the mainland visa-free list, but with a few important extras like <strong>the US, Mexico, Philippines, and Indonesia</strong> that aren't on the mainland 30-day list.</p>
      <div class="bg-emerald-50 border-l-4 border-emerald-400 rounded-r-xl p-5 mb-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-emerald-800"><strong>💡 Quick note:</strong> Unlike the mainland visa-free policies, Hainan's list covers a broader range (59 vs 50 countries). If your country isn't on the <a href="/en/visa/visa-free/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">mainland visa-free list</a>, check if it's on the Hainan list — it might be your only visa-free option for China.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">See the <a href="/en/visa/visa-free/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">full 59-country breakdown by region →</a></p>
    </section>

    <!-- When to Visit -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="when-to-visit" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">When to Visit Hainan</h2>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
              <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Month</th>
              <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Temp</th>
              <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Rain</th>
              <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Crowds</th>
              <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Verdict</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Nov–Mar</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">20–28°C</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">Low</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">High</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-emerald-600">🌟 Best time — dry, warm, perfect beach weather</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Apr–Jun</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">25–32°C</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">Moderate</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">Low</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-amber-600">👍 Good — hotter but fewer tourists</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Jul–Oct</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">26–32°C</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">High (typhoon season)</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">Low</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-red-600">⚠️ Rainy — cheap flights but check typhoon forecasts</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Peak tourist season:</strong> Chinese New Year (Jan/Feb) and National Day Golden Week (Oct 1–7) — avoid if you can.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Why Visit -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="why-visit" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">🏝️ Why Visit Hainan?</h2>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Hainan is China's answer to Hawaii — a tropical island with white-sand beaches, lush rainforest, and a laid-back vibe you won't find anywhere else on the mainland. It's the only part of China where you can truly escape the city and relax by the ocean. Plus, with visa-free access for 59 countries, it's the easiest entry point to China for many travelers.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- How Many Days -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="how-many-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">📅 How Many Days Do You Need?</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">
        <li><strong>3–4 days (standard):</strong> Sanya beaches, seafood, and one day trip to Haikou or a rainforest hike</li>
        <li><strong>5–7 days (comfortable):</strong> Split between Sanya and Haikou, add Boao and Wuzhishan hiking</li>
        <li><strong>7+ days (deep dive):</strong> Full island loop via high-speed rail — explore the entire coastline</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Top Attractions -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="attractions" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">🎯 Top Attractions</h2>

      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">🏖️ Sanya — The Beach Hub</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">Sanya is where most tourists go. Think palm trees, white sand, and high-end resorts.</p>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Yalong Bay</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Best beach on the island. Clear water, soft sand, surrounded by resorts.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Dadonghai Bay</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">More local vibe, cheaper hotels, lots of seafood restaurants right on the beach.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Haitang Bay</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Quieter, more upscale. Home to Atlantis Sanya (water park + aquarium).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Wuzhizhou Island</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Day trip destination for snorkeling and crystal-clear water.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Nanshan Temple</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Home to the 108-meter Guanyin statue — the tallest in the world.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Yanoda Rainforest</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Jungle hiking with waterfalls and canopy walks.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Luhuitou Park</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Sunset views over Sanya from the hilltop park.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">🏛️ Haikou — The Capital</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">More culture, less beach.</p>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Volcanic Geopark</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Hike up an extinct volcano crater — a rare geological experience right near the city.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Qilou Old Street</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Arcaded buildings from the 1920s. A great photo spot with a mix of colonial and Chinese architecture.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Hainan Museum</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Learn about the Li and Miao minority cultures that make Hainan unique.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Mission Hills</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Massive resort complex with golf, hot springs, and a film studio theme park.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">🗺️ Beyond the Two Main Cities</h3>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Boao</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Annual Asia Forum town with a beautiful coastal road.</p>
        <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-400 p-3 rounded-r-lg text-sm text-blue-800">
          💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> If you're interested in cutting-edge medical treatments combined with a resort stay, Boao Lecheng is China's only medical special zone with access to overseas-approved drugs and therapies not yet available on the mainland.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Wuzhishan (Five Finger Mountain)</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Best hiking on the island — climb the iconic five peaks for panoramic jungle views.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Xinglong</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Tropical botanical garden and coffee plantations — a relaxing day trip from Sanya or Haikou.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Bawangling</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Wild rainforest home to the rare Hainan gibbon — one of the rarest primates on Earth.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Getting Around -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="getting-around" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">🚇 Getting Around Hainan</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>High-speed rail:</strong> Hainan has a circular high-speed rail line that connects Haikou, Boao, Sanya, and most towns. Trains run frequently and are cheap (Haikou → Sanya ~¥100, 1.5 hours).</li>
        <li><strong>Taxis / Didi:</strong> Call a ride easily through the <a href="/en/transport/didi/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">DiDi app</a> or via Alipay/WeChat mini programs.</li>
        <li><strong>Car rental:</strong> Possible with an International Driving Permit + Chinese translation</li>
        <li><strong>Buses:</strong> Cheap but slow, routes cover most tourist spots</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Where to Stay -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="where-to-stay" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">🏨 Where to Stay</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">Hainan resorts are generally cheaper than equivalent quality in Southeast Asia. A ¥500/night room in Yalong Bay often includes breakfast and has a private beach area.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-6">
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">💰 Budget (¥100-200)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Dadonghai area hostels (Sanya) · Qilou area guesthouses (Haikou)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">💰💰 Mid-Range (¥300-600)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Yalong Bay mid-range resorts (Sanya) · Mission Hills area hotels (Haikou)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">💰💰💰 Premium (¥800+)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Atlantis, Edition, Ritz-Carlton — Haitang Bay (Sanya) · Hilton, Marriott city center (Haikou)</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What to Eat -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="what-to-eat" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">🍜 What to Eat in Hainan</h2>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Hainan's food is all about fresh tropical flavors — lots of seafood, coconut, and rice.</p>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Wenchang Chicken</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Hainan's most famous dish. Poached chicken with ginger-scallion sauce. Find it at any local restaurant in Haikou.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Jiaji Duck</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Slow-cooked duck with a rich broth. A must-try in Boao.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Hainan Noodles</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Thin rice noodles in broth or dry style. A breakfast staple found everywhere.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Seafood</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Fresh crabs, prawns, clams, fish — grilled or steamed. Head to the Sanya seafood market, where you buy fresh and they cook it on the spot.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Coconut Rice</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Sticky rice cooked in coconut milk. A sweet and fragrant treat found at night markets.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Qingbuliang</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">A refreshing dessert soup with coconut milk, beans, fruits, and ice. Perfect for hot Hainan days — find it at Sanya street stalls.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visa-Free Rules -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="visa-rules" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Visa-Free Rules — Exactly What You Need to Know</h2>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
              <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Question</th>
              <th class="text-left px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-700">Answer</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">How long can I stay?</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">Up to <strong>30 days</strong> — counted from the day after you arrive</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Do I need a tour group?</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3"><strong>No</strong> — independent solo travelers are fine</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Can I extend?</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">Possibly, apply at the local immigration office in Hainan</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Can I visit mainland China?</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3"><strong>No</strong> — this policy only covers Hainan island</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Can I enter Hainan, go to Hong Kong, then come back?</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">Yes — each entry resets the 30-day clock</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">What if I overstay?</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3">Fines + possible entry ban. Don't risk it.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Entry requirements:</p>
      <ol class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-gray-700">
        <li>✅ Passport valid for 6+ months</li>
        <li>✅ Return or onward ticket within 30 days</li>
        <li>✅ Hotel booking (recommended)</li>
        <li>✅ Arrival card (given on the plane or <a href="/en/visa/arrival-card/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">fill online</a>)</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Practical Tips -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="tips" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Practical Tips for Hainan</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>Pay with Alipay or WeChat Pay</strong> — set them up before you fly. Most places in Hainan are cashless. See our <a href="/en/payment/payment-guide/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">How to Pay in China</a> guide.</li>
        <li><strong>VPN is still needed</strong> — Google, WhatsApp, Instagram won't work without it. <a href="/en/life/best-vpns/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Set up a VPN</a> before you arrive.</li>
        <li><strong>SIM card / eSIM</strong> — buy one online (airalo, Holafly) or at the airport. See our <a href="/en/life/best-sim-esim/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">SIM guide</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Language</strong> — English is not widely spoken in Hainan outside of resorts. Have Google Translate or Pleco ready.</li>
        <li><strong>Sunscreen + mosquito repellent</strong> — both are essentials year-round.</li>
        <li><strong>Tipping</strong> — not expected. See our <a href="/en/payment/tipping/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tipping guide</a>.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Guides -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 id="related" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">📚 Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/en/visa/visa-free/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100 no-underline">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">China Visa-Free Countries List (2026)</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">See the full 59-country list for Hainan</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/visa/arrival-card/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100 no-underline">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">How to Submit Your Arrival Card Online</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Step-by-step guide with screenshots</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/cities/beijing-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100 no-underline">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">Beijing Travel Guide</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">China's capital city guide</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/cities/shanghai-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100 no-underline">
